Subject: [PATCH] Cert-book event-driven trigger on LIVE (supersedes #264)

#264's work re-cut from LIVE 1a32f9532 with its conflicts resolved:
- book-key sizing: LIVE's fold_book_aliases wins; #264's book_shares split is dropped
  (decision_core.book_shares and its call site removed, its test rewritten to assert the fold).
- LIVE's _allocator_book name; #264's consumed-decision trace lives on _allocator_book.consumed.
- manage_open_positions: LIVE's refused-sleeve exit management, keyed by #264's owned_tags.
- main: LIVE's deadman/hold/daily-loss/OCO gates after #264's new_risk_gate.
- pf_allocator world cache: #264's world_population/world_fingerprint with LIVE's whole-state
  digest as the decision_state component; LIVE's source pin updated to the merged code.
- allocator_proof, gateway_drill, test_gateway_adapter: both sides kept.
- decision journal: LIVE's rows untouched; #264's two decisions re-journalled as
  D-20261113-001/002 via scripts/context.py decide.

Squashed for the seal carrier (one commit on a LIVE ancestor) from 5eeff5186b627422c1be6c427b423b532b71dbcf, tree identical:
- v2: harness and reviewer-pin fixes after the #264 re-cut
- v2: off-roster tag test no longer expects the shared-tag log (tags are distinct now)
- v2: off-roster TTL close matches on owned_tags, never an exact single tag
- v2: WORLD_CACHE_MAX_AGE_S cites its cadence derivation (3600 s, hourly heavy clock)
- v2: an unmeasured growth curve keeps the 20% heat floor (seal HOLD H1)
- v2: headwind test bounds at min(survival, target floor)

